cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these reproducibility materials, please cite this archive using these metadata."

title: "Reproducibility Data and Code for Reduced-Order Modelling of Magnetically Coupled Engineering Systems"

type: dataset

authors:
  - family-names: "Markov"
    given-names: "Paul D."

abstract: >-
  Numerical data, Python notebooks, machine-readable evidence, supplementary
  audit records, and publication-figure materials supporting the manuscript
  "Reduced-Order Modelling of Magnetically Coupled Engineering Systems".
  The archive contains scalar and coupled plasma-surrogate identification
  results, leave-one-perturbation-out verification, nominal tangent-linearisation
  recovery, Savitzky-Golay preprocessing sensitivity, corrected
  Euler-Bernoulli structural benchmark results, canonical cross-domain
  comparisons, complete input-output frequency-response metrics, and
  best-achievable structural damping analyses. The plasma component is a
  controlled stochastic numerical surrogate and does not constitute
  experimental or high-fidelity physical plasma validation.

version: "1.0.0"

date-released: "2026-08-25"

repository-code: "https://github.com/unified-reality-framework/MEA_ROM_reproducibility_v1.0"

url: "https://github.com/unified-reality-framework/MEA_ROM_reproducibility_v1.0"

license: GPL-3.0-only

keywords:
  - reduced-order modelling
  - state-space identification
  - modal analysis
  - plasma dynamics
  - structural dynamics
  - transfer functions
  - frequency-response analysis
  - reproducibility
  - leave-one-perturbation-out verification
  - Savitzky-Golay sensitivity
